    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37107" width="470" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- OVP2 output voltage:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="37107" width="1080" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="2">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">V.OVP2_out</e>
        <e type="operand">V.OVP1_out</e>
        <e type="operand">2.5</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operand">2.3</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
        <contract>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
        </contract>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">29.89</e>
        </result>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37324" width="1560" height="51" color="#444444" fontSize="9" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">The auxiliary winding SUPPLIES VCC (2026-09-25): there is no external rail. It feeds VCC through a Zener-referenced emitter follower and a bypass diode (DS 5.1.8), and the ZCD divider below. n.aux_max and k.auxr are the ST tool&#x27;s test for an auxiliary</p>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">winding wired straight to VCC; with the regulator in between, the 25 V limit applies to the regulator OUTPUT, and k.VCC in section 14c tests that instead. This is a deliberate difference from the ST workbook.</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37383" width="470" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- Maximum auxiliary-to-secondary turns ratio (direct feed only):</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="37383" width="1080" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="4">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">n.aux_max</e>
        <e type="operand">25</e>
        <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operand">V.OVP2_out</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">0.8364</e>
        </result>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37444" width="470" height="35" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">[PICK] SELECTED auxiliary-to-secondary ratio:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="37444" width="1080" height="35" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffff80" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math>
      <input>
        <e type="operand">n.aux</e>
        <e type="operand">1</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37487" width="1560" height="23" color="#444444" fontSize="9" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">1.0: the lowest whole-turn ratio that keeps the regulator in regulation at the end of hold-up (k.RBZ, 14c); 0.5 puts VCC below the HVSU threshold, 1.5 raises everything the regulator burns by half.</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37518" width="470" height="54" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- auxiliary ratio under the direct-feed limit (&gt;1 only if wired</p>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">straight to VCC):</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="37518" width="1080" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="3">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">k.auxr</e>
        <e type="operand">n.aux_max</e>
        <e type="operand">n.aux</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">0.836</e>
        </result>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37580" width="470" height="35" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- Auxiliary turns in series (whole number):</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="37580" width="1080" height="35" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="2">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">N.aux</e>
        <e type="operand">n.aux</e>
        <e type="operand">N.s</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">2.00</e>
        </result>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37623" width="1560" height="23" color="#444444" fontSize="9" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">TOTAL, all cores together. It has to be a whole number, and nothing else here checks that. With N.x &gt; 1, wind one turn on every unit and series as many as this needs; the rest stay open.</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37654" width="470" height="35" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- Auxiliary winding nominal voltage:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="37654" width="1080" height="35" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="2">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">V.aux</e>
        <e type="operand">n.aux</e>
        <e type="operand">V.out</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
        <contract>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
        </contract>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">25.00</e>
        </result>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37697" width="1560" height="23" color="#444444" fontSize="9" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">holds only while the winding is coupled to the SECONDARY: wind it in triple-insulated wire over the secondary (section 14c).</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37728" width="470" height="35" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- Auxiliary voltage at OVP2:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="37728" width="1080" height="35" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="2">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">V.aux_OVP2</e>
        <e type="operand">n.aux</e>
        <e type="operand">V.OVP2_out</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
        <contract>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
        </contract>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">29.89</e>
        </result>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37771" width="470" height="35" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- ZCD divider bias current at OVP1:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="37771" width="1080" height="35" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffff80" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math>
      <input>
        <e type="operand">I.bias</e>
        <e type="operand">120</e>
        <e type="operand" style="unit">μA</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37814" width="470" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- Lower ZCD resistor:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="37814" width="1080" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="3">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">R.ZCD_L</e>
        <e type="operand">2.3</e>
        <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operand">I.bias</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
        <contract>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">kohm</e>
        </contract>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">19.167</e>
        </result>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37875" width="470" height="35" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">[PICK] SELECTED lower ZCD resistor:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="37875" width="1080" height="35" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffff80" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math>
      <input>
        <e type="operand">R.ZCD_L_sel</e>
        <e type="operand">19</e>
        <e type="operand" style="unit">kohm</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37918" width="470" height="35" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">[PICK] SELECTED upper ZCD resistor:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="37918" width="1080" height="35" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffff80" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math>
      <input>
        <e type="operand">R.ZCD_H_sel</e>
        <e type="operand">220</e>
        <e type="operand" style="unit">kohm</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37961" width="1560" height="23" color="#444444" fontSize="9" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">E24 value ABOVE the calculated one, so OVP1 sits clear of the ripple peak.</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="37992" width="470" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- Upper ZCD resistor:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="37992" width="1080" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="2">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">R.ZCD_H</e>
        <e type="operand">R.ZCD_L_sel</e>
        <e type="operand">n.aux</e>
        <e type="operand">V.OVP1_out</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operand">2.3</e>
        <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operand">1</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">-</e>
        <e type="bracket">(</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
        <contract>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">kohm</e>
        </contract>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">208.17</e>
        </result>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="38053" width="1560" height="23" color="#444444" fontSize="9" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">connect the auxiliary winding so ZCD is POSITIVE when LOUT1 is on. The opposite polarity causes destructive hard switching.</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="38084" width="470" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- divider ratio actually fitted:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="38084" width="1080" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="4">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">r.ZCD</e>
        <e type="operand">R.ZCD_H_sel</e>
        <e type="operand">R.ZCD_L_sel</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operand">1</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">+</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">12.5789</e>
        </result>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="38145" width="470" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- OVP1 the fitted divider really gives:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="38145" width="1080" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="2">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">V.OVP1_act</e>
        <e type="operand">2.3</e>
        <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operand">n.aux</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operand">r.ZCD</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
        <contract>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
        </contract>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">28.93</e>
        </result>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="38206" width="1560" height="23" color="#444444" fontSize="9" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">[97]  only the RATIO sets the threshold, so both resistors must be the selected parts.</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="38237" width="470" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- OVP2 the fitted divider really gives:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="38237" width="1080" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="2">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">V.OVP2_act</e>
        <e type="operand">2.5</e>
        <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operand">n.aux</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operand">r.ZCD</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
        <contract>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
        </contract>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">31.45</e>
        </result>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="38298" width="1560" height="23" color="#444444" fontSize="9" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">[98]</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="38444" width="470" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- Output-voltage overshoot the core must survive:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="38444" width="1080" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="4">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">k.OVsat</e>
        <e type="operand">V.OVP2_act</e>
        <e type="operand">V.out</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">1.2579</e>
        </result>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="38505" width="470" height="35" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- Test current on the vendor specification:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="38505" width="1080" height="35" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="2">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">I.sat_spec</e>
        <e type="operand">I.sat_eq</e>
        <e type="operand">k.OVsat</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
        <contract>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">A</e>
        </contract>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">15.61</e>
        </result>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="38548" width="1560" height="23" color="#444444" fontSize="9" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">rounded UP to a whole ampere on the specification sheet. It is well under the tank peak I.Lr_pk and that is correct - with the secondary OPEN there is no ampere-turn cancellation, so this current makes the same core flux that I.Lr_pk makes in service.</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="38579" width="470" height="35" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- ZCD voltage at the end of start-up:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="38579" width="1080" height="35" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffff80" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math>
      <input>
        <e type="operand">V.ZCD_SUend</e>
        <e type="operand">1.36</e>
        <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="38622" width="470" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- Output voltage where start-up hands over:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="38622" width="1080" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="2">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">V.out_SUend</e>
        <e type="operand">V.ZCD_SUend</e>
        <e type="operand">2.3</e>
        <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operand">V.OVP1_act</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
        <contract>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
        </contract>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">17.11</e>
        </result>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="38683" width="470" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- OVP1 against the target (near 1):</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="38683" width="1080" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="3">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">k.OVP1</e>
        <e type="operand">V.OVP1_act</e>
        <e type="operand">V.OVP1_out</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">1.052</e>
        </result>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="38760" width="1560" height="27" color="#0f2a44" fontSize="12" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-size: 12px;">14c. VCC from the auxiliary winding - 2 T and a Zener regulator</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="38795" width="1560" height="51" color="#444444" fontSize="9" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">aux winding -&gt; D.aux -&gt; C.aux -&gt; NPN emitter follower (base held by a Zener fed through R.BZ from C.aux) -&gt; bypass diode -&gt; VCC pin and C.VCC. The bypass diode is the one DS 5.1.8 asks for: it keeps the HVSU charge current out of the regulator. The same</p>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">winding drives the ZCD divider above.</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="38854" width="470" height="35" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">[DS] VCC turn-on threshold (rising):</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="38854" width="1080" height="35" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffff80" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math>
      <input>
        <e type="operand">V.CC_on</e>
        <e type="operand">17</e>
        <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="38897" width="470" height="35" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
